{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541040-monteparnas-technocratic-structure","id":1541040,"title":"Monteparnas' Technocratic Structure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-26T16:36:59-07:00","id":1541040,"title":"Monteparnas' Technocratic Structure","content":"I'm currently running a Mage game, the first non-crossover I ever did, and I want to present some of my takes for this chronicle and see what others think of them. <br /> The following is my version of a more complete chart for ranks within the Technocratic Union, which is relevant for some PCs directly and to the group as a whole for some of my planned plots.<br /> <br /> My assumption for the Awakened population in this game is that they're exceedingly rare, and most members of any Awakened group are actually Sleepers, like Sorcerers and Acolytes, even people that simply buy into their Paradigm, but otherwise have only mundane skills.<br /> <br /> For the purpose of defining concepts, I'll use the following:<ul><li><b>Believers</b>: people who buy into a Paradigm. They're so into it as to not count as witness, but otherwise are just Sleepers. They can use some simple Wonders, though;</li> <li><b>Extraordinary Citizens/Acolytes</b>: people who study a Paradigm enough to, under the right circumstances, replicate Effects. They're the ones who can use Wonders/Devices and can also learn individual Rotes as Static effects;</li> <li><b>Sorcerers</b>: people who follow proper rules for sorcery plus access to buying Rotes as Static powers. They're usually more powerful, but still far from a proper Awakened of similar level.</li> </ul>As a final observation, the distinction between Acolytes, Sorcerers and the Awakened is frequently a tricky one. An Acolyte may theoretically know Rotes of any level, in any number, and with sizeable dice pools, not to say be really knowledgeable about their magical Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Without further ado:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TECHNOCRACY FLOWCHART </b><ul><li><b>0- Contractors</b></li> <li><b>1- Unenlightened Support</b></li> <li><b>2- Unenlightened Specialist</b></li> <li><b>3- Extraordinary Citizens </b></li> <li><b>4- Initiated Operatives</b></li> <li><b>5- Autonomous Operatives</b></li> <li><b>6- Special Agents</b></li> <li><b>7- Supervisors</b></li> <li><b>8- Symposium Supervisors</b></li> <li><b>9- Horizon Special Teams</b></li> <li><b>10- Horizon Managers</b></li> <li><b>11- Old Masters</b></li> <li><b>12- Control</b></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> 0- <b>Contractors</b><br /> The tendrils of the Union's influence reach markets and institutions through unaffiliated service providers. While the Conspiracy can and do keep tabs on those people, they're just doing their mundane work to clients that sink back into obscurity in short notice.<br /> <br /> 1- <b>Unenlightened Support</b><br /> Those people work directly for the Technocracy, even if most don't know. From janitors to minor management and mundane security services, day to day activities in the many installations owned by the Union require a lot of mundane work. Some know who their employers are, or at least have a hint, most do not, but all are paid by Technocratic money and get a few perks out of it.<br /> <br /> 2- <b>Unenlightened Specialist</b><br /> People come in every shade of usefulness, and some have hard to come by skills, networks and access. Those people have high dice pools (7+) and Backgrounds, rare Merits, an advantage not tied to game terms, or a combination thereof, and simply put take a lot of resources to establish or replace. Many are Believers and know to whom they work, either by deduction, being informed, or even because they're made in a lab, but many do not, or have only a vague hunch.<br /> <br /> 3- <b>Extraordinary Citizens</b><br /> While it isn't proof of competency, being able to put superscience and hypertech to use is an invaluable ability, so those who can are either at leadership positions or working under the guidance of the Enlightened. Techno-sorcerers and Enlightened personnel start at this rank once identified, where they're trained and evaluated.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 1</b></i><br /> <br /> 4- <b>Initiated Operatives</b><br /> Here is where the Enlightened circles of the Conspiracy begin, with those who proved they're a cut above to understand and develop superior science. Techno-sorcerers of great skill become researchers, managers and directors at facilities, while Enlightened personnel are welcomed to Boot Camp, where they'll transition from their former, mundane lifes and identities to become fullfledged Technocrats.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 2</b></i><br /> <br /> 5- <b>Autonomous Operatives</b><br /> At this level, agents of the Union are expected to be able to work the Will of the Conspiracy all by themselves. They are fully trained and well versed in the secret work, able to either do exceptional work alone or in Amalgams, or to command a research team to achieve greater heights.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 3 to 5</b></i><br /> <br /> 6- <b>Special Agents</b><br /> Operatives with great experience or exceptional mundane skills receive special attention and are selected for important missions. Some serve the Union by leading Amalgams or lesser personnel in such missions, but specially difficult or sensitive cases may require a full Amalgam of this level.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 3 to 5</b></i><br /> <br /> 7- <b>Supervisors</b><br /> The managers of the Technocratic Union on Earth, Supervisors are the linchpins of whole networks of Amalgams, projects and resources. Each is a conspiracy on their own, their responsibilities going as far as they're individually capable of reaching.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 4 to 6</b></i><br /> <br /> 8- <b>Symposium</b><br /> While they also use the word in its usual meaning with great frequency, in Technocratic parlance a Symposium is the highest institution of the Union within this world. One for each continent and few others with specialized agendas, they number in eight at most, each composed by one Supervisor of each Convention. Strictly speaking this rank is only applied to the institution itself, but few lesser Supervisors dare to think they are in equal terms with a Symposium member.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 4 to 6</b></i><br /> <br /> 9- <b>Horizon Special Teams</b><br /> The most Enlightened agents of the Union are rewarded with access to its best facilities, for whatever purpose the agent wants it. Training grounds, laboratories, factories the size of small nations, places where there's no such a thing as &quot;impossible&quot;, usually on carefully customized space stations. On top of that, even pet projects are treated as vital research by the Symposia on Earth. Now only the very top of the Union has a say on what you do.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 5 to 8</b></i><br /> <br /> 10- <b>Horizon Directors</b><br /> The very top as far as identifiable people go. A dozen or so incredible masterminds that define the strategy, long term goals, and evaluate the success of the entire Conspiracy on a multi-worlds scale. Or sometimes just glorified Supervisors with too much power and no idea of how things are actually going, or how people work.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 5 to 8</b></i><br /> <br /> 11- <b>Old Masters</b><br /> If they still exist, those five are the very top of each Convention, Enlightened beyond measure and each more an ideal to achieve, a living representation of the collective Will of their Convention, than a boss. If and when they have a directive to pass, they do directly to whom they want, whichever rank that be, through means of their own instead of through hierarchy.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 9+, they may be Oracles, they may not exist as individual entities anymore.</b></i><br /> <u>In my game: they died decades ago when they became a part of the new entity Control.</u><br /> <br /> 12- <b>Control</b><br /> Above the individual Masters is all of them together, or the thing that once was all of them together. Control is capable of manifesting its Will with absolute proof of its identity, through several special identifiers. Control is the Union in no uncertain terms. Control may be the apex of Enlightenment, a mad inhuman thing, a simple reflection of expectation, or all of those.<br /> <i><b>Typical Enlightenment: 10+. Think about the plus.</b></i><br /> <u>In my game: Control is a Godhead. It was born from the Union, but is ultimately a distinct thing.</u><ul><li>\u200c<b>Unenlightened Rank:</b></li> </ul>Many Enlightened members of the Union have personal assistants, security detachments, and representatives who are either Sleepers or just Initiated, but are trusted and competent at their jobs.<br /> <br /> Those underlings have access to information and political clot far above the rank they would be at otherwise, and even authority over some agents as they speak in the name of their boss.<br /> <br /> Such assistants are effectively 2 ranks below their masters as standard fare, be it informal or official standing.<br /> <br /> Depending on their role and if there's no objection from a higher authority, they can be assigned a rank 1 below their boss or even temporarily the same Rank, if they're trusted with overseeing an operation in their name.<ul><li>\u200c<b>Unranked Enlightenment:</b></li> </ul>Enlightenment isn't always obvious, and its rarity makes probing everyone unfeasible. On top of that, just as some agents prove themselves more than capable to receive high responsibilities, some are simply too incompetent to be paired with their equals.<br /> <br /> Members ranked below expectations are rarer than the opposite, and usually this is a temporary condition. Between fringe theories, pet projects and the sheer size of the sea of regular scientific production, noticing Extraordinary or Enlightened work may take some time, even years.<br /> <br /> While incompetent agents aren't a rare thing by themselves, losing rank due to this is. An agent must have a very unique combination of lack of results, useful but subpar skills and loyalty to be either demoted or kept at a low rank relative to their Enlightenment, instead of dealt with in some other way.<ul><li><b>\u200cA Column, Not A Pyramid:</b></li> </ul>This may be a bit of an exaggeration, but it is important to notice that this structure doesn't necessarily have exponential increments from one tier to the other, and in my game this isn't the case, indeed.<br /> <br /> At any given moment there may be Symposium Supervisors participating in more than one, so they can have multiple Symposia with their small numbers, while other Supervisors don't greatly outnumber them.<br /> <br /> Enlightened personnel are rare and precious, even the stupid ones, and most operations run mostly or solely on the hands of Sleepers. And even then, the resources are stretched thin, the Union puts a facade of complete control of the world, but this is far from the reality.<br /> <br /> You do you, of course, but as a rule of thumb feel free to only put in play the characters you need, and run your extras as Sleepers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T11:29:56-07:00","id":1541473,"title":"","content":"Currently working on a project outlining the upcoming Technocratic civil war and I may steal some of what you've laid out here to help structure my thinking.<br /> <br /> My interest is piqued though. &quot;<u>In my game: Control is a Godhead. It was born from the Union, but is ultimately a distinct thing.</u>&quot; I would like to know more!<br /> <br /> In my project I take the &quot;Control is a gestalt matrix of leading technocrats&quot; as canon. Briefly, I'm incorporating several &quot;original sins&quot; of the modern Union that center on the Great Housekeeping and the implementation of CONTROL in the late 1800's. Turns out most of the arch-mages that comprise that gestalt matrix were some combination of white, British, and male. Most of them came up during the Industrial Revolution and tended to favor rapid and drastic changes to society and the economy regardless of the disruption this may cause in the lives of individual sleepers and even whole sleeper populations. Folks for whom coal mine collapses and children work houses were just the price paid for progress. I also posit that the Technocracy engaged in something like Project: Paperclip after the World War II, setting the stage for increased nephandic (and mundane) corruption.<br /> <br /> So we have Control with sub-standard initial conditions whose inhumanity and disconnection grows as new generations technocrats with outdated ideals are added. It all kinda snowballs into the cartoonishly evil TU from first edition which then slowly, over the course of several decades (and editions) is attempting to right itself.<br /> <br /> Is your control similar? The phrase &quot;born of the Union but distinct from it&quot; is so tantalizing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-03T15:17:52-07:00","id":1541489,"title":"","content":"My idea starts from the concept of the gestalt entity, but that it is just the first step in the evolution of this new thing. Beyond that, there's the metaphysical weight of everything people both inside and outside the Union think about the True Masters\u2122, good or bad.<br /> <br /> Control is the God of Conspiracy, so to speak. It is the archetypal Grand Master for every conspiracy theory. To spread the idea of a secret cabal rulling the world is to sing hymns to it.<br /> <br /> As a godhead, Control isn't bound just to the Union, it may influence or contact others at will, and will do so for its own purposes. It may even be behind the Rogue Council and other conspiratorial activities, or at least part of it. It doesn't inhabits any Construct, but wanders the world just as other godheads do.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing, while this god doesn't exist just to please followers, ultimately it doesn't rule more than it is empowered to. While it does have access to the Union's many conditionings, most of what the Technocrats did since the turn of the 19th to the 20th century, they did by themselves, out of their expectations about Control more than from actual orders.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Control is an alien god with no unified agenda. It has many aspects and avatars that may very well act against each other, as long as they follow the general idea of a secret master, good or evil. Although my players will have a chance to find all this out and maybe convince this god to settle on a given course, as it is now Control works for and against everyone, including corruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T07:29:35-07:00","id":1541527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1541040-monteparnas-technocratic-structure?p=1541489#post1541489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea starts from the concept of the gestalt entity, but that it is just the first step in the evolution of this new thing. Beyond that, there's the metaphysical weight of everything people both inside and outside the Union think about the True Masters\u2122, good or bad.<br /> <br /> Control is the God of Conspiracy, so to speak. It is the archetypal Grand Master for every conspiracy theory. To spread the idea of a secret cabal rulling the world is to sing hymns to it.<br /> <br /> As a godhead, Control isn't bound just to the Union, it may influence or contact others at will, and will do so for its own purposes. It may even be behind the Rogue Council and other conspiratorial activities, or at least part of it. It doesn't inhabits any Construct, but wanders the world just as other godheads do.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing, while this god doesn't exist just to please followers, ultimately it doesn't rule more than it is empowered to. While it does have access to the Union's many conditionings, most of what the Technocrats did since the turn of the 19th to the 20th century, they did by themselves, out of their expectations about Control more than from actual orders.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Control is an alien god with no unified agenda. It has many aspects and avatars that may very well act against each other, as long as they follow the general idea of a secret master, good or evil. Although my players will have a chance to find all this out and maybe convince this god to settle on a given course, as it is now Control works for and against everyone, including corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked all of it, very well done. One thing that I would change is that I wouldn't allow for any given &quot;Higher Supervisor&quot; (Rank 8) to be a member of more than one Symposium at a time, but that's just my personal opinion.<br /> <br /> As for Control, I loved this, and you gave me an idea that may be cool to play at, and it is to have a secret cult of Control inside the Union, whose main purpose is to &quot;achieve Unity&quot;, which literally means becoming part of the Gestalt consciousness... Which happens on rare occasions (blessed be those that have achieved Unity!).<br /> <br /> This would also play well with the Union's origin, replacing the original worship of the Cabal of the Pure Though (of God) for the worship of this &quot;false idol&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, there would be the danger of derailing the Technocracy, since in the end of all of it, at the very core, it would become a Conspiracy inside of a Conspiracy inside of a Conspiracy whose REAL purpose is to just spread mayhem in the world, and all the talk about &quot;protect the Masses&quot; would just be a mask, and make the Technocracy be undeniably EVIL. But I still like that idea nevertheless, I don't know if you'll agree - surely, that &quot;cult&quot; would only ever be present at the higher levels, thus those idealistic technocrats at the base are only just unwilling and unknowning pawns of their demented higher ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T13:16:54-07:00","id":1541545,"title":"","content":"I quite like your formulation <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>. I may yoink parts of it for my own project. Particularly the &quot;god of conspiracy&quot; line and multitudinous and sometimes conflicting plots (very God Machine like in that way). Since my Control is over-indexed with NWO compared to the other conventions it may work with my canon as well. Part of its madness is perpetrating inhumanity due to having uploaded a significant number of morally and ethically compromised arch-mages. But maybe its also engaging in multiple conspiracies within and outside the Union. Its smashing part of the Union against each other (and outside forces) to see which is strongest. Or it has some other reason and we are either too humane or to bounded by time and lifespans to see the 5 dimensional chess it is playing.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Civil War (going down the way it planned with the combatants it has selected) is part of its plan all along?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T15:39:50-07:00","id":1541548,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you both liked it!<br /> <br /> This version of Control may have any goal at a given time, with no obligation to any. A cult or more of Control could be anything, from people with a specific vision of what the Master should be or do, to those who want power for power's sake, thinking that serving this ideal or god will put them next to the apex of the pyramid.<br /> <br /> Later I'm thinking about using this godhead even with other splats, to see how I can tweak things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}